-- `l4 batch` re-prints a module and evaluates the printed text, so a printer
-- that drops the brackets around an operand changes the answer with no
-- diagnostic. Each export here puts one kind of operand inside an AND; the
-- expected answers are those of the #EVAL lines below, which `l4 run` gives.

GIVEN x IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
negate x MEANS NOT x

@export A disjunction inside a conjunction
GIVEN p IS A BOOLEAN
      q IS A BOOLEAN
      r IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`or under and` MEANS (p OR q) AND r

@export A negation inside a conjunction
GIVEN p IS A BOOLEAN
      q IS A BOOLEAN
      r IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`not under and` MEANS (NOT p) AND q

@export An implication inside a conjunction
GIVEN p IS A BOOLEAN
      q IS A BOOLEAN
      r IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`implies under and` MEANS (p IMPLIES q) AND r

@export A conditional inside a conjunction
GIVEN p IS A BOOLEAN
      q IS A BOOLEAN
      r IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`if under and` MEANS (IF p THEN q ELSE TRUE) AND r

@export A function call inside a conjunction
GIVEN p IS A BOOLEAN
      q IS A BOOLEAN
      r IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`call under and` MEANS (negate p) AND q

#EVAL `or under and` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#EVAL `not under and` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#EVAL `implies under and` FALSE FALSE FALSE
#EVAL `if under and` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#EVAL `call under and` FALSE FALSE FALSE
